{"id": "intl_paper-2026-11-23-013", "date": "2026-11-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["intl_paper"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "International Paper opts to split off, not sell, DS Smith", "content": "<p>The choice &ldquo;maximizes value&rdquo; for both companies, said CEO Andy Silvernail on Monday. IP now projects a substantially lower cash dividend payout in 2027, following a period of &ldquo;burning cash&rdquo; and sluggish demand, an analyst said.</p>", "sources": [{"name": "packaging_dive", "url": "https://www.packagingdive.com/news/international-paper-split-not-sell-ds-smith/875452/", "type": "rss"}]}
